# probes/reverdict.fixture — a census table used only to drive the identity law.
#
# CensusReverdict's own javadoc names its identity falsifier: invoked with the
# same table on both sides it must print every delta as zero and STABLE. That
# property is about the COMPARISON and not about the multiverse, so the lane
# drives it from ten frozen rows rather than by growing twenty universes on
# every push — the wall-clock argument #1162 made for keeping the table run
# out of the bench. These rows were captured from SeedAtlas 1 20 6000 at
# f26af14 and are inputs to a law, not a claim about the world: nothing here
# is re-derived from a run, so a lawful digest move does not stale them.
